<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Quantitative results of homography estimation in visible-infrared dataset. The best and second of each category are masked as bold and underline, respectively.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="Sx4.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results:</span> As shown in Table <a href="#Sx4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Implementation Details ‣ Experiments ‣ DistillMatch: Leveraging Knowledge Distillation from Vision Foundation Model for Multimodal Image Matching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, DistillMatch achieves significantly higher AUC than other algorithms at all thresholds for the cloudy-cloudy and cloudy-sunny datasets. The performance on the cloudy-sunny dataset is lower than on the cloudy-cloudy dataset, due to increased image feature variation from light and temperature differences, which makes matching and pose estimation more challenging. Figure <a href="#Sx3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Category-Enhanced Feature Guidance Module ‣ Methodology ‣ DistillMatch: Leveraging Knowledge Distillation from Vision Foundation Model for Multimodal Image Matching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (a) illustrates the qualitative results.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx4.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Homography Transformation Estimation</h3>

<div id="Sx4.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dataset and Evaluation Metrics:</span> To evaluate the homography estimation performance of DistillMatch, we conducted experiments on four visible-infrared datasets covering distinct scenarios: (1) UAV remote sensing images <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. 2022</a>)</cite>, (2) indoor scenes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">SMT/COPPE/Poli/UFRJ 2021</a>)</cite>, (3) nighttime conditions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">González et al. 2016</a>)</cite>, and (4) haze and mist scenes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie and Jin 2023</a>)</cite>. We randomly generate a unique homography matrix and apply it as GT to the original image. The homography matrices include random translations of <math id="Sx4.SSx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-10\%,10\%]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-10\%,10\%]</annotation></semantics></math>, rotations of <math id="Sx4.SSx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-20,-20]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-20,-20]</annotation></semantics></math>, scaling of <math id="Sx4.SSx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.8,1.2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.2</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.8,1.2]</annotation></semantics></math>, shear angles of <math id="Sx4.SSx3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-0.1,0.1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-0.1,0.1]</annotation></semantics></math>, and perspective transformations of <math id="Sx4.SSx3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-0.003,0.003]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.003</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0.003</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-0.003,0.003]</annotation></semantics></math>. For UAV remote sensing dataset, we evaluate matching performance by calculating the mean reprojection error of four corner points, adopting AUC under thresholds of 3, 5 and 10 pixels. For the other datasets, AUC is computed at thresholds of 5, 10 and 20 pixels.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results:</span> As evidenced by Table <a href="#Sx4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Relative Pose Estimation ‣ Experiments ‣ DistillMatch: Leveraging Knowledge Distillation from Vision Foundation Model for Multimodal Image Matching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Figure <a href="#Sx3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Category-Enhanced Feature Guidance Module ‣ Methodology ‣ DistillMatch: Leveraging Knowledge Distillation from Vision Foundation Model for Multimodal Image Matching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> (a), DistillMatch achieves significantly higher AUC values than competing methods across most thresholds on all datasets, with the performance gap widening progressively as thresholds increase. Figure <a href="#Sx3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Category-Enhanced Feature Guidance Module ‣ Methodology ‣ DistillMatch: Leveraging Knowledge Distillation from Vision Foundation Model for Multimodal Image Matching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>(a) demonstrates that DistillMatch precisely aligns feature points between source and target images. This alignment preserves geometric consistency and structural integrity in transformed images despite scale variations, viewpoint distortions, and rotational changes.</p>
</div>
